        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Writing intellectual history requires choices: What counts as an \"idea\"? What is its relevant\ncontext? How do you avoid reading present concerns into past texts (anachronism)? The major\nmethodological schools disagree sharply, and their debates parallel disputes in the philosophy\nof history and interpretation theory."
